WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.242 --> 00:00:02.927
(laughing)

00:00:02.927 --> 00:00:04.410
- Helena Bonham Carter

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.243
- How are you doing?

00:00:05.243 --> 00:00:06.190
- Very well thanks, how are you?

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.023
- I'm fine.

00:00:07.023 --> 00:00:09.109
How are you enjoying your
acting career so far?

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.960
(laughing)

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:11.920
- I'm enjoying it, thanks.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.520
- Let's say that I'm your fairy godmother,

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:14.567
and you'd say,

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:17.727
"Hello fairy godmother,
can you just adjust things

00:00:17.727 --> 00:00:20.070
"and take a few of the bad bits away?"

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.760
What would the bad bits that
you want me to take away be?

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.613
- I'd quite like, I love doing the job,

00:00:24.613 --> 00:00:26.810
love working with people you work with,

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.430
I'd quite like no one to ever watch it.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.760
- That's exactly what I think, too.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.973
- 'cause that's where it gets ruined.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.483
- I prefer not to watch it,

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:38.690
and not anyone to watch it.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.580
It's kinda nice up til now,
we've been in this bubble,

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.270
and this is never gonna come out.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.230
But now its suddenly gonna come out.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.760
- [Olivia] Yeah, that's
where it all goes wrong.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.200
- What's the question you
don't want me to ask you?

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.017
- Tell us some funny stories from on set.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.683
I hate that one.
- Yeah, or can you tell me,

00:00:52.683 --> 00:00:54.526
how did you research
- No, they're my funny stories

00:00:54.526 --> 00:00:56.531
- for this part?
- with my friends on set.

00:00:56.531 --> 00:00:57.600
- Research the part (laughs).

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.470
- Can you tell me about that,
how did you approach the part?

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.973
- How did you approach the part, Helena?

00:01:00.973 --> 00:01:01.957
(laughing)

00:01:01.957 --> 00:01:02.790
You tell me.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:03.670
- It's very funny 'cause I think

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:04.987
we're utterly different on that bit.

00:01:04.987 --> 00:01:06.700
Aren't we, we are quite different.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.940
I think we're quite
similar in some things.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.380
But, I think I do everything

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.772
and you don't do anything.

00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:14.605
(laughing)

00:01:14.605 --> 00:01:15.820
But, she's amazing.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.836
I mean you are, you're a phenomenon.

00:01:17.836 --> 00:01:21.730
But I think you're quite
private about what you do.

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:22.563
- Maybe that's what it is

00:01:22.563 --> 00:01:23.690
that makes it sound better.
- So in fact,

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:25.780
I think you do a lot but you just pretend

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.590
that you don't do anything.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:29.800
I think you must have
a photographic memory.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:30.652
Do you have a photographic memory?

00:01:30.652 --> 00:01:31.485
- No.

00:01:31.485 --> 00:01:32.318
- How do you learn your lines?

00:01:32.318 --> 00:01:33.151
Just out of, I know,

00:01:33.151 --> 00:01:34.780
a lot of people don't
like talking about it

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.270
and I know you don't
like talking about it,

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.944
'cause there's a sort of

00:01:37.944 --> 00:01:38.777
- But?

00:01:38.777 --> 00:01:39.610
- But,

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:41.400
but how do you actually?

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.520
- I don't do any
differently to anyone else.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.535
- How do you know?

00:01:44.535 --> 00:01:45.368
(laughing)

00:01:45.368 --> 00:01:46.460
- Well, I presume,

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.190
because I don't have a photographic memory

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:49.023
- You don't?

00:01:49.023 --> 00:01:50.220
- No, so you do have to sit there and

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.870
short scenes I won't bother
learning until on the day.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:53.703
- Really?

00:01:53.703 --> 00:01:55.370
- Because I don't think
there's room in my head to.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:57.100
Some people learn stuff for a whole week.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:57.933
I can't do that.

00:01:57.933 --> 00:02:00.960
- See, if I left it to the
day, I'd get too panicked.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.260
- Only a short scene.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.300
- Even a short scene.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.870
I can't, it won't stick.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.210
I'm gonna have cue cards everywhere,

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.043
it's gonna be a disaster.

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:08.440
- You won't, just
literally, a little scene,

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.350
maybe if you had a couple of lines,

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.507
you wouldn't have to learn
that in advance, would you?

00:02:11.507 --> 00:02:14.870
- No, I wanna feel, I think I just

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.200
I can't absorb.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.290
- I quite like the panic.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.258
- Do you like the adrenalin?

00:02:19.258 --> 00:02:20.091
- Yeah.

00:02:20.091 --> 00:02:20.924
- I've got a few friends

00:02:20.924 --> 00:02:21.757
who like the adrenalin.
- I love the end of the day.

00:02:21.757 --> 00:02:23.990
You know the end of a
day when they haven't,

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.000
everyone's a little bit panicked

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.421
and everyone's, we've
got to finish at six.

00:02:27.421 --> 00:02:28.254
I love that.

00:02:28.254 --> 00:02:29.820
- [Helena] And you can
only do a few takes?

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:30.780
- I love that.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:31.613
- Yeah, you like that bit.

00:02:31.613 --> 00:02:33.357
Except when you're knackered
at the end of the day

00:02:33.357 --> 00:02:35.160
and you just
- It's like a coffee, isn't it

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.690
it sort of really picks you up.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.840
- So you're a bit of an
adrenalin junkie possibly?

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:40.673
- Maybe.

00:02:40.673 --> 00:02:42.910
(laughing)

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:43.870
I've never thought that about myself.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:45.420
- OK the best bit and the worst bits.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.270
So what are the best bits of
this job and the worst bits?

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:51.000
- The best bits are

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.260
- [Helena] The acting bit?

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.410
- well, making friends.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.570
That's always the best bit.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:57.530
'Cause like minded people,

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.340
you always find them on a set, don't you?

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.990
Cast and crew.
- Yeah.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:01.823
- Love that.

00:03:01.823 --> 00:03:03.300
I love it when it's well written.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.400
I love being in a scene that's
really beautifully written.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.127
- Yeah, makes us look better.
- And you feel it.

00:03:07.127 --> 00:03:07.960
And it's great.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:09.557
- And it takes off.

00:03:09.557 --> 00:03:11.527
- And you can feel that
(inhaling and exhaling).

00:03:11.527 --> 00:03:13.190
Worst bits?

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.940
5am get ups.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:15.773
Errrrr

00:03:15.773 --> 00:03:17.560
- It's just not possible, not feasible.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.380
- I'm much better at 5am,

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.833
I mean at being on time than I am,

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.490
once the kids are wake them I'm screwed.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.650
- So, actually in a way it's
better that you wake up at five

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:27.610
'cause they're not--

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:29.120
- Well then I'm just, I
wake up and 10 minutes later

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.293
I'm in my car.
- You have your solitary time.

00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:31.610
You can have your own time.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.950
How to juggle those two.
- I don't really like

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.160
my own time.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.706
- No, I love my own time,

00:03:36.706 --> 00:03:38.030
see that's where we differ.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.286
We are very different in that way.

00:03:39.286 --> 00:03:40.119
- What's your best and worst?

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.744
- The best bit is when I read a script

00:03:41.744 --> 00:03:43.820
and it's great writing.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.230
And I go "I could do
this" and "I could that"

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:48.150
and, I've got got all
these ideas and possibility

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.473
is just endless.
- I don't have any ideas.

00:03:50.473 --> 00:03:52.020
(laughing)

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.240
- That's the difference
between you and me.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.560
So I get too many ideas
and I get option-itus

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:57.910
but it's just so exciting.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.790
And then I dream and start
dreaming I could do this

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:00.937
and I could do that
- You get option-itus?

00:04:00.937 --> 00:04:01.770
- Option-itus?

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.727
- So you pick different ways of doing it?

00:04:03.727 --> 00:04:05.220
- All the time.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.710
Yeah, I love choice.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:07.970
We could do it this way,
we could do it that way,

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.220
and the better the writing,

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:10.570
the more choices you have,

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:11.703
and that excites me.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.710
- Gosh, I see that quite differently.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:16.250
- Totally different, isn't it interesting?

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.900
- So the better the
writing, the more I think

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.396
I know exactly where I'm meant to go.

00:04:20.396 --> 00:04:22.037
And, if the writings bad then I think

00:04:22.037 --> 00:04:23.207
"oh God, I've got lots of ideas."

00:04:23.207 --> 00:04:24.392
- No, that's true.

00:04:24.392 --> 00:04:25.973
That's true too.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:29.773
The good thing about,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.750
I find the worst writing you've gotta find

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.360
one way or one choice that makes it work.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.623
The better the writing,

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.580
you could do it many, many different ways.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.849
- And it will still be good?

00:04:41.849 --> 00:04:43.250
- It will still be good
and then it's up to you

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:45.277
to go like hang on.
- Yeah, maybe you're right.

00:04:45.277 --> 00:04:48.630
- But it's sort of, so the
best bit is before you do it,

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.810
the worst bit is when you watch it.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:50.882
- Yeah, when you get the job,

00:04:50.882 --> 00:04:51.820
the best bit is hearing.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.588
- Is when getting the job.

00:04:53.588 --> 00:04:54.421
(exclaiming and cheering)

00:04:54.421 --> 00:04:55.953
(laughing)

00:04:55.953 --> 00:04:59.130
And then, from then on, the
idiocy of this profession is

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.230
you really wanna job,

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.063
then you get the job

00:05:01.063 --> 00:05:01.970
and then you're racing
through the schedule

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:04.287
going like "when have I got my days off?".

00:05:04.287 --> 00:05:05.120
(laughing)

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.323
It's so stupid.

00:05:06.323 --> 00:05:08.065
- I think every actor's
like that, aren't they?

00:05:08.065 --> 00:05:09.400
- We're pathetic.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.920
But the worst bit is actually watching.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.418
I can't bear watching,
can you watch yourself?

00:05:12.418 --> 00:05:13.251
- No I don't mind
watching, I just don't want

00:05:13.251 --> 00:05:14.627
anyone else to watch
it that's the problem.

00:05:14.627 --> 00:05:16.560
I don't mind watching.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.730
- You don't mind watching yourself?

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:18.563
- No.

00:05:18.563 --> 00:05:19.610
- That's so interesting.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:20.443
- Do you mind?

00:05:20.443 --> 00:05:21.276
- I hate it.

00:05:21.276 --> 00:05:22.109
- Why?

00:05:22.109 --> 00:05:23.590
- [Helena] It's never what
I thought it was gonna be.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.423
I had all these dreams.
- I know,

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:25.256
and there's definitely
moments when I think,

00:05:25.256 --> 00:05:27.420
oh I wish I'd done that differently.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.570
- But, I'm always trying
to get out of myself.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:30.980
- I think that I'm thinking,

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:33.310
I probably see it as worse
- Oh you do.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.143
- as somebody else does.

00:05:34.143 --> 00:05:36.070
- No we all can't judge ourselves.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:37.670
And also I don't think we can,

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.900
it's a very, I feel like
I'm in a sort of like,

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.810
it's a bit of a
narcicisstic way of watching

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:44.070
because you're always
going like me, me, me.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.040
And in fact, you're not seeing the story,

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.110
so you don't see what,

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:49.073
you're not seeing the context.

00:05:49.073 --> 00:05:52.620
There's so much that
perverts our perception.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.370
- I do love watching,

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.470
to watch, for example,

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.380
scenes that you've done with Ben Daniels,

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.430
that I wasn't present at.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:00.382
I love watching what
everyone else has done.

00:06:00.382 --> 00:06:02.333
- Yeah, I like scenes that I'm not in.

00:06:03.611 --> 00:06:06.000
- Because we're lucky we get to learn

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.553
to do different things
like horse riding, or

00:06:10.218 --> 00:06:11.560
have you--
- What have you had to learn?

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:12.740
Walk?

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:13.600
(laughing)

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.000
- I can't do that!
- No.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.180
That's something we have
in common, we can't walk.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.194
- Yeah we can't, we
both walk like farmers,

00:06:18.194 --> 00:06:19.027
no offense to farmers
- We can't walk in high heels.

00:06:19.027 --> 00:06:21.030
- but it's not royalty
is meant to walk like.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.125
- No, no, no we can't do high heels.

00:06:23.125 --> 00:06:23.958
- Look.

00:06:23.958 --> 00:06:25.438
Look at us both, here you are.
- (laughing)

00:06:25.438 --> 00:06:26.646
- We've got platform trainers

00:06:26.646 --> 00:06:28.580
and sandals, the pair of us.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:29.573
- Any wide shot,

00:06:30.469 --> 00:06:31.813
it's not fortunate.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.750
- Now I have to say, I
thought I was bad in heels,

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.400
then I met you.
- (laughing)

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.570
- It's amazing.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:39.583
Bambi on ice.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.680
- They're implements,
they're stupid things,

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.815
them as a torture and they're disabling.

00:06:45.815 --> 00:06:47.747
- They can be very pretty, very pretty.

00:06:47.747 --> 00:06:49.640
- They can be pretty, but they hurt.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.280
And I can't stand up.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:53.567
And I can't get from A to B.

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:56.329
(laughing)

00:06:56.329 --> 00:06:58.300
And honestly, Amy, who I love

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:00.411
- She's our incredible

00:07:00.411 --> 00:07:01.500
wardrobe designer
- she's not given me one shoe

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:02.740
that fits my foot.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.190
- Oh my god I've seen
- I love her.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.190
- at least 20 shoes in your--

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:07.520
- What about your shoes?

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.070
Do they fit your foot?

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.070
- Well, they're alright.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.286
- She likes you better then.

00:07:11.286 --> 00:07:12.119
(laughing)

00:07:12.119 --> 00:07:12.995
She's got it in for my feet!

00:07:12.995 --> 00:07:13.828
- No, but she's trying, she's had about

00:07:13.828 --> 00:07:15.370
20 shoes out for you, maybe your--

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.150
- Argh, they don't work.
- Unless they're trainers,

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.110
- you're not happy.
- I mean they're normal feet

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:19.180
they're reasonably normal.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.850
- They're very little feet.

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:22.840
- But they're honestly,

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:25.496
they seem to be a puzzle,
an impossibility for her.

00:07:25.496 --> 00:07:26.800
(laughing)

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.680
The bits I don't like are sitting still

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.680
having hair and make up done.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:31.513
They're brilliant,

00:07:31.513 --> 00:07:33.410
but you know that you've
gotta be there for them

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.243
and still

00:07:34.243 --> 00:07:36.822
and I can't sit still very
well for two and a half hours.

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:40.246
Plus my music choice is
not helpful (laughing)

00:07:40.246 --> 00:07:42.890
- (sighs) So we all, all of us
are in a makeup van together.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:43.743
- All in a row.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:45.730
- And sure enough

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:47.423
- Lots of chats.

00:07:48.593 --> 00:07:49.700
This is at five o'clock in the morning.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:53.470
- I particularly enjoy annoying Tobias,

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:55.438
'cause he's quite quiet and quite sensible

00:07:55.438 --> 00:07:56.590
and he's working
- And he wears his earphones.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:58.316
- Wears his earphones and I keep going

00:07:58.316 --> 00:07:59.907
(whining voice) "TM!"

00:07:59.907 --> 00:08:01.330
And asking him questions and he,

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.530
I know that he's just being sweet

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:04.543
'cause he actually
wants to go "fuck off!".

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:08.730
- Beam me up, Scotty.
- Bless him, he has

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:10.078
to sit between us, that's awful.

00:08:10.078 --> 00:08:11.035
- It's not good for him.

00:08:11.035 --> 00:08:14.100
- But, Helena has the most extraordinary

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:14.933
- Bad

00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:16.728
(laughing)

00:08:16.728 --> 00:08:19.770
- Extraordinarily bad playlist
for in the makeup van.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.963
- It's perfect, she thinks its spa music.

00:08:22.864 --> 00:08:24.130
Shall we play a little?

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.017
We could actually--
- Oh no!

00:08:25.017 --> 00:08:25.991
(laughing)

00:08:25.991 --> 00:08:28.005
No, don't put anyone through it.

00:08:28.005 --> 00:08:31.537
We sometimes text each
other, behind you, going

00:08:31.537 --> 00:08:33.600
"what the fuck is this
that she's playing?'.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:34.433
- Ah, is that what happens?

00:08:34.433 --> 00:08:36.862
And then there was a
song that was really nice

00:08:36.862 --> 00:08:37.930
- it was sort of lulling,
- It wasn't,

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:39.685
it was a ridiculous
- the yurt song?

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:40.518
(singing with a thick accent)

00:08:40.518 --> 00:08:41.351
♪Welcome in my yurt song ♪

00:08:41.351 --> 00:08:43.980
(laughing)

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:44.813
- But we don't wanna have,

00:08:44.813 --> 00:08:46.500
if you had your way,
- We had it every day

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.350
for eight months.
- You would be in a festival

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:49.240
from five o'clock.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:53.416
- I bought Sue, Sue David my
makeup artist, disco lights.

00:08:53.416 --> 00:08:54.743
(humming dance music)

00:08:54.743 --> 00:08:55.576
- We had a disco.
- But that's not

00:08:55.576 --> 00:08:57.370
what everybody wants early in the morning.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.203
- I do understand that.

00:08:58.203 --> 00:08:59.800
- Your energy is prodigious, mine isn't.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:02.160
I spend most of my time
horizontal and having snoozes.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:03.627
- At lunch time today I said,

00:09:03.627 --> 00:09:04.940
"Hellie shall we have lunch together?"

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.437
And she said "you can have 10
minutes of eating and talking

00:09:07.437 --> 00:09:09.127
"and then I will be lying
down and you can lie down

00:09:09.127 --> 00:09:11.301
"next to me but silence after that."

00:09:11.301 --> 00:09:13.059
Well, no thanks.

00:09:13.059 --> 00:09:13.892
(laughing)

00:09:13.892 --> 00:09:14.943
I'll go and chat to everyone else.

00:09:14.943 --> 00:09:16.736
- Well you can chat to other, you know,

00:09:16.736 --> 00:09:19.400
you've got amazing stamina.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.660
We have different energy levels.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.360
I come up and then I die.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:24.733
And then I need to have a snooze.

00:09:24.733 --> 00:09:27.035
And my hot water bottle.

00:09:27.035 --> 00:09:29.020
- And I like a snooze, but
not when we're all together!

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:30.430
I want to chat.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:33.263
- But then, you last, you've
got all these reserves.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:36.909
And we've also got
another six months, Colly.

00:09:36.909 --> 00:09:39.373
(laughing)

00:09:39.373 --> 00:09:41.540
- Eight I think it's eight actually.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:44.979
- I think we should have a
snooze at lunch, pace yourself.

00:09:44.979 --> 00:09:45.812
- No!

00:09:47.137 --> 00:09:47.970
I don't want to.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.330
- We've got the new young blood.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:50.660
- [Olivia] Yeah, I've got the young blood.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:53.563
That'll be a test to
our stamina, won't it?

00:09:53.563 --> 00:09:55.350
It might turn out--
- I think you'll be fine.

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:57.600
(laughing)

00:09:58.872 --> 00:10:01.872
But they're all great and hilarious.

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:06.257
Erin is hilarious.
- Oh god, she's brilliant.

00:10:07.694 --> 00:10:10.340
- It is fun to watch
everybody, and see what they

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.480
and Josh is brilliant.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:12.723
- I love that Erin,

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:14.403
she's (in cockney accent)

00:10:14.403 --> 00:10:15.378
"Aright?

00:10:15.378 --> 00:10:16.211
"How's it goin?

00:10:16.211 --> 00:10:17.044
"Yeah, yeah, yeah, nice."

00:10:17.044 --> 00:10:18.335
and then she suddenly becomes

00:10:18.335 --> 00:10:19.710
- (in posh British accent)
"Hello".

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:20.543
(laughing)

00:10:20.543 --> 00:10:21.670
- She is amazing.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:22.763
- She is amazing.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:25.943
- I do find sometimes, you know

00:10:25.943 --> 00:10:28.068
when you're working with
someone who's really good,

00:10:28.068 --> 00:10:30.685
and I'm like "oh that was good"

00:10:30.685 --> 00:10:31.779
oh shit it's my turn!

00:10:31.779 --> 00:10:33.987
(laughing)

00:10:33.987 --> 00:10:37.320
- Do you remember the first
scene, that was funny.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.628
- No, what was the first scene?

00:10:38.628 --> 00:10:40.400
- The first scene we
actually did together.

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:41.240
- No.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.963
- You actually put ear plugs in

00:10:42.963 --> 00:10:43.820
so you didn't have to listen.
- (gasps) Sorry!

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:46.460
- No it was very funny, I
thought it was hilarious.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:49.009
- That sounds rude, that was
not as rude as it sounds.

00:10:49.009 --> 00:10:52.080
'Cause she was saying
very upsetting things

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:55.524
and my character was meant to
be much stronger than I am,

00:10:55.524 --> 00:10:57.190
and I kept going (groaning)

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:59.583
and you were like, that's not
how the Queen would react.

00:10:59.583 --> 00:11:00.416
(laughing)

00:11:00.416 --> 00:11:02.283
So I had to listen, they cleverly,

00:11:02.283 --> 00:11:03.580
the brilliant sound department,

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:06.790
came up with they tuned
into the shipping forecast

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.184
and I had it in my ears.

00:11:08.184 --> 00:11:09.017
- It was extraordinary.

00:11:09.017 --> 00:11:09.850
So she wasn't listening to me.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.420
I had this long spiel

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.386
and I could see Olivia's
sort of far away look

00:11:14.386 --> 00:11:16.271
- Going (robotic voice)
south utsire, north utsire--

00:11:16.271 --> 00:11:18.160
- And then she'd look at me
'cause she had one line to say

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.586
and then go "hmm?".

00:11:19.586 --> 00:11:22.190
(laughing)

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:24.740
And then Marion was being the
Queen Mother in front of me

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.520
and then there was this one
on the shipping forecast

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:29.840
I thought "this is very, very funny".

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:32.803
But then you did take
the ear plugs out, after.

00:11:32.803 --> 00:11:35.397
- See, I didn't do it in
every scene we had together.

00:11:35.397 --> 00:11:38.340
- No but you have and you
haven't been telling me.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.248
(laughing)

00:11:40.248 --> 00:11:41.081
- I'm listening to

00:11:41.081 --> 00:11:42.108
(sings electronic music)

00:11:42.108 --> 00:11:44.123
- All your festival music.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:46.147
I know you don't really
like talking about it

00:11:46.147 --> 00:11:47.844
but you are amazing.

00:11:47.844 --> 00:11:48.920
- You're talking about
work again, aren't you?

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.550
- Yeah, yeah.

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:53.710
'Cause it's funny, it is very private,

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:56.140
I don't want to pry
where it's too private.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:58.890
But is there anything
that you do to get into

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.076
do you do any thinking?

00:12:02.076 --> 00:12:04.326
(laughing)

00:12:05.698 --> 00:12:07.222
About this part?

00:12:07.222 --> 00:12:08.370
- Yes.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:09.510
- But on an unconscious level?

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:10.343
- But it's written so beautifully

00:12:10.343 --> 00:12:12.890
and you've got great voice coaches

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:17.510
and then there's not an
awful lot else to do.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:18.890
Tell me the funniest thing you've done

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:20.720
to get into character.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:21.810
I know the answer already,

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:23.010
but I just want you to tell everyone.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:24.140
- Which one, the farting?

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:24.973
Or the?

00:12:24.973 --> 00:12:25.806
(laughing)

00:12:25.806 --> 00:12:27.190
'Cause that's not intentional.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:29.940
What for Margaret?

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:30.773
- Yes.

00:12:31.806 --> 00:12:32.639
- Not sure.

00:12:32.639 --> 00:12:33.472
Head back,

00:12:33.472 --> 00:12:34.433
I do a bit of a head back.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.290
- Who did you approach to help you get--

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:38.123
- Oh the medium?

00:12:38.123 --> 00:12:41.883
- Yeah, I still think that's really funny.

00:12:41.883 --> 00:12:42.938
I love you very much.

00:12:42.938 --> 00:12:43.965
(laughing)

00:12:43.965 --> 00:12:46.465
Do you know someone in the
last press junket said,

00:12:47.465 --> 00:12:50.097
"so we heard that Helena
approached a medium,

00:12:50.097 --> 00:12:51.663
"did you approach a medium?".

00:12:51.663 --> 00:12:53.480
No, 'cause the Queens's still alive.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:54.810
- [Helena] Somebody yesterday did say,

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:57.790
really, really clever,
lovely man photographer,

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:00.347
said "so did you get to meet her?

00:13:00.347 --> 00:13:01.547
"Did you have to meet?".

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:03.910
Mm kind of.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:05.480
She did.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:06.313
- Kind of.

00:13:07.675 --> 00:13:11.830
- But, I'm very anal so no stone unturned,

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:14.230
so I thought well why
not, give it a whirl.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.870
Meet a medium and see
what they come up with.

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:18.030
And actually,
- And was it helpful though?

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:19.090
- I think it was.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:22.690
'Cause the first thing that she said was

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:23.599
- The medium or Margaret?

00:13:23.599 --> 00:13:26.930
- It was via the medium,
obviously Margret wasn't there,

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.810
but the medium, who is a friend of mine,

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:30.800
who is a psychic and
generally helps people

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:31.693
- And gets paid?

00:13:32.999 --> 00:13:36.571
- She did get paid but
not an inordinate amount.

00:13:36.571 --> 00:13:38.373
I know where your heads going.

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:41.870
Take total advantage of me, but,

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:44.500
so the first thing that
she'd said, apparently,

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:45.580
she said, "Oh, Margaret's here."

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:46.576
and I said, "oh really"

00:13:46.576 --> 00:13:48.500
'cause I was actually
doing it for other reasons

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.407
and she said "oh well, we
might as well talk to her

00:13:50.407 --> 00:13:51.240
"since she's come'

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:53.330
and said, "she's in full regalia"

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:56.547
she said, "she does like
the fact that I'm playing,

00:13:56.547 --> 00:13:58.397
"I'm a better choice than the other actor

00:13:58.397 --> 00:13:59.267
"they were thinking of."

00:13:59.267 --> 00:14:00.920
(gasps)

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:01.753
So that's good.

00:14:01.753 --> 00:14:03.903
- Unless the other actor's watching this.

00:14:04.802 --> 00:14:06.439
- I don't know, no I know.

00:14:06.439 --> 00:14:08.453
But that's a very typical thing

00:14:08.453 --> 00:14:09.740
that she gives you a compliment

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.795
and also sort of puts you
down at the same time.

00:14:11.795 --> 00:14:14.095
She said it was about
time that I scrubbed up,

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.298
that's very Margaret, she said--

00:14:17.298 --> 00:14:20.210
- Oh what is it, that your
friend just wanting to say?

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.043
- Maybe.

00:14:23.016 --> 00:14:24.140
Because funnily enough,

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:26.120
when she contacted my great granny,

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:27.380
my great granny had the same thing

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.557
so it's "enough of this
eccentric dressing,

00:14:29.557 --> 00:14:31.360
"can you just be elegant now.".

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:32.310
- You are elegant.

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:33.143
- Today I'm elegant.

00:14:33.143 --> 00:14:34.070
- You're so beautiful.

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:36.725
- Oh thank you, but not every day.

00:14:36.725 --> 00:14:38.530
- You are, you're always very elegant.

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:39.810
- No, I'm not.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:40.650
- Well I think you are.

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:41.483
- Thank you.

00:14:41.483 --> 00:14:43.708
The one thing that I thought,
this is a good note from her,

00:14:43.708 --> 00:14:47.727
she said, "remember that
the cigarette holder

00:14:47.727 --> 00:14:50.131
"is as much a weapon for expression

00:14:50.131 --> 00:14:54.900
"as just satisfying my an addiction.".

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:55.733
- Oh, that's good.

00:14:55.733 --> 00:14:56.933
- That's pretty articulate.

00:14:59.878 --> 00:15:00.711
That was about it.

00:15:00.711 --> 00:15:02.010
Scrub up.

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:03.322
- So rude.

00:15:03.322 --> 00:15:04.330
(laughing)

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.163
- Scrub up.

00:15:05.163 --> 00:15:07.426
And then once I did meet
her, that was another thing,

00:15:07.426 --> 00:15:09.760
and I did think that's pretty ironic.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:10.670
'Cause she said to me

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:11.503
- You did meet?

00:15:11.503 --> 00:15:13.730
- I met her years ago,
before she died, obviously.

00:15:15.579 --> 00:15:16.412
In my early thirties and she said,

00:15:16.412 --> 00:15:19.110
"Oh you are getting better, aren't you.".

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:22.073
And that was a very typical, now I got,

00:15:22.073 --> 00:15:23.970
there was something rather
ambivalent about her,

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:26.330
she complimented but she'd take it away.

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:28.800
And she's always slightly
difficult to place

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:30.850
and it's that prickly sort of atmosphere.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:35.270
- Which is what makes her
such a wonderful character.

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:38.573
- She's complicated and she's not easy.

00:15:38.573 --> 00:15:42.447
Not easy to be I don't
think but fun to play.

00:15:42.447 --> 00:15:44.940
And you can do it many, many ways

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.220
and it would be appropriate.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:48.710
- But you see, we don't
have many ways with

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:49.900
the people that we're playing because,

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:52.655
I mean I couldn't play the Queen Welsh.

00:15:52.655 --> 00:15:55.769
- You definitely couldn't play
her (in Welsh accent) Welsh.

00:15:55.769 --> 00:15:58.374
But you could try (in foreign accent)

00:15:58.374 --> 00:16:00.577
and that is not Welsh is it, I
don't know what we are going.

00:16:00.577 --> 00:16:02.407
- You're going all over Europe.

00:16:04.457 --> 00:16:05.290
- No, the Queen,

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:07.152
the whole point about the
Queen is so consistent.

00:16:07.152 --> 00:16:07.985
- Yeah.

